.TH XUEIFY 1 2026-10-23 "xueify @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xueify \- lightweight notification daemon for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xueify
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xueify
implements the freedesktop.org Desktop Notifications specification and shows
each notification as a rounded card in the bottom-right corner of the screen,
drawn on a wlr-layer-shell surface. It needs a compositor that supports
.B zwlr_layer_shell_v1
(Hyprland, Sway, river, niri, labwc and others).
.PP
While no notification is on screen the daemon sleeps in
.BR poll (2)
and holds no buffers or timers.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.TP
.B Timeouts
Notifications close after the timeout requested by the sender, or after 5 seconds
when the sender leaves it to the server. Critical notifications stay until dismissed.
Hovering a card pauses its timeout; leaving restarts it.
.TP
.B Stacking
Up to five cards are shown, newest at the bottom; the rest wait in a queue.
.TP
.B Replacing
A notification that names an existing id in
.I replaces_id
or shares an
.I x-canonical-private-synchronous
(or
.IR x-dunst-stack-tag )
hint is updated in place.
.TP
.B Images
.IR image-data ,
.I image-path
and
.I app_icon
are honoured in that order and cropped to a square cover.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
.B Left click
Invokes the
.I default
action, if the sender offered one, and closes the card.
.TP
.B Right click
Closes the card.
.TP
.B Middle click
Closes every card, including queued ones.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.Notifications.service
D-Bus activation file.
.TP
.I xueify.service
systemd user unit that runs the daemon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the compositor goes away, 1 when the session bus or the compositor cannot
be used or another daemon already owns
.BR org.freedesktop.Notifications .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify-send (1)
.PP
https://github.com/ouxan/xueify
